---
import { priceRequests } from './keys-model.mjs';
interface Props { kind: 'identity' | 'fields' | 'schema' | 'negative' }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const titles={identity:'Four questions, how many answers?',fields:'Changing a pair of fields',schema:'The same bytes, two meanings',negative:'Remembering that nothing was found'};
---
<figure class="cache-figure key-figure" data-keys={kind} aria-label={titles[kind]}>
 <span class="figure-title">{titles[kind]}</span>
 {kind==='identity' && <>
  <div class="key-requests">{priceRequests.map(r=><div><b>{r.id} · {r.tenant}</b><span>{r.currency} · {r.group}</span><strong>{r.currency} {(r.amount/100).toFixed(2)}</strong></div>)}</div>
  <fieldset><legend>Include in the key, alongside the product</legend><div class="controls"><label><input type="checkbox" data-field="tenant"/> Shop</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-field="currency"/> Currency</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-field="group"/> Price group</label></div></fieldset>
  <p class="key-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓ same key, same saved answer ↓</p>
  <div class="key-buckets" data-buckets><div class="key-bucket"><code>mug</code><p>First saved answer: north · EUR · retail · 18.00</p><p>A fits; B, C and D receive the wrong answer.</p></div></div>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">The first request fills the entry. Others with the same key reuse its answer.</p>
  <figcaption>Requests arrive A, B, C, D, then repeat once. Each letter below a stored answer is one request. A cross marks an answer with the wrong shop, currency or price group. The first request for each key fills it; no entry changes or expires.</figcaption>
 </>}
 {kind==='fields' && <>
  <div class="controls"><label>Write the replacement <select data-mode aria-label="How to write the replacement"><option value="separate">Two HSET commands</option><option value="hash">One HSET, both fields</option><option value="json">One SET, whole JSON value</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="field-pair" data-pair><div><span>currency</span><strong data-currency>EUR</strong></div><div><span>amount in cents</span><strong data-amount>1800</strong></div></div>
  <div class="key-output"><span>A reader retrieves both fields now</span><strong data-displayed>EUR 18.00</strong><span data-pair-status>Complete old answer</span></div>
  <div class="controls"><button data-play>Play writes</button><label class="scrubber">Write step <input data-step aria-label="Field update step" type="range" min="0" max="2" step="1" value="0" /></label><button data-reset>Reset</button></div>
  <p class="key-command"><code data-command>Starting copy</code></p>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">Start with EUR 18.00. The intended replacement is USD 20.00.</p>
  <figcaption>Each slider position is a point between commands. The reader retrieves the pair in one HMGET, or one GET for JSON. A single multi-field write has no visible half-written state; two separate writes do. This says nothing yet about whether the source value being written is fresh.</figcaption>
 </>}
 {kind==='schema' && <>
  <div class="controls"><label>Writer <select data-writer aria-label="Writer value format"><option value="1">v1 · euros</option><option value="2" selected>v2 · cents</option></select></label><label>Reader <select data-reader aria-label="Reader value format"><option value="1">v1 · euros</option><option value="2">v2 · cents</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="key-translation"><div><span>Written to Redis</span><code data-written-key>price:mug</code><strong data-bytes>1800</strong><small data-written-unit>Writer means cents</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div data-decoder><span>Reader asks for</span><code data-read-key>price:mug</code><strong data-decoded>€1800.00</strong><small data-read-unit>Reader interprets euros</small></div></div>
  <div class="controls"><label><input data-versioned type="checkbox"/> Put the format version in the key</label></div>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">A successful lookup returns bytes the reader misinterprets.</p>
  <figcaption>There is one saved value, written by the selected writer. A versioned key makes the incompatible reader miss. In a real rolling deployment, old and new entries can coexist under their respective keys.</figcaption>
 </>}
 {kind==='negative' && <>
  <div class="controls"><label>First source lookup <select data-outcome aria-label="Source lookup outcome"><option value="missing">Succeeds: no such product</option><option value="found">Succeeds: product found</option><option value="failed">Fails: source times out</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="controls"><label><input data-negative type="checkbox"/> Save a confirmed “not found” answer</label></div>
  <div class="key-translation"><div><span>After the first request</span><small>Value in Redis</small><code data-entry>absent</code></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span>Second request</span><strong data-second>Read source again</strong><small data-response>Not found</small></div></div>
  <div class="origin-work" aria-label="Source reads"><span>Source reads</span><i data-origin-one>1</i><i data-origin-two>2</i></div>
  <p class="readout" data-status aria-live="polite">Two requests repeat the same unsuccessful search.</p>
  <figcaption>Both requests ask for the same authorised product view. There is no intervening creation, deletion or expiry. A source failure is never converted into a “not found” answer. The example models application policy, not a Redis feature that discovers absence automatically.</figcaption>
 </>}
 <noscript><p>The initial example and its caption remain visible. Enable JavaScript to change the inputs.</p></noscript>
</figure>
<script>import './keys-and-values.js';</script>
<style>
 .key-requests{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.6rem;}
 .key-requests>div{border-top:2px solid var(--blue);padding:.7rem .3rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);}
 .key-requests b,.key-requests span,.key-requests strong{display:block;font-size:.8rem;}
 fieldset{border:0;padding:0;margin:1.5rem 0 .5rem;}legend{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);}
 .key-arrow{text-align:center;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin:.8rem 0;}
 .key-buckets{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.7rem;}
 .key-buckets:has(> :only-child){grid-template-columns:1fr;}
 .key-buckets :global(.key-bucket){border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:6px;padding:.85rem;background:var(--color-surface);}
 .key-buckets :global(code){display:block;font-size:.72rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
 .key-buckets :global(p){font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin:.6rem 0;}
 .key-buckets :global(.assigned){display:flex;gap:.35rem;flex-wrap:wrap;}
 .key-buckets :global(.assigned span){display:inline-block;border:1px solid var(--teal);padding:.15rem .35rem;border-radius:3px;font-size:.75rem;}
 .key-buckets :global(.assigned .wrong){border-color:var(--coral);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--coral) 15%,var(--color-surface));}
 .field-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;max-width:380px;margin:2rem auto;}
 .field-pair>div{border:2px solid var(--teal);border-radius:5px;padding:1rem;text-align:center;transition:background .2s;}
 .field-pair span,.key-output span{display:block;font-size:.8rem;}
 .field-pair strong{font-size:1.6rem;}
 .field-pair.mixed>div{border-color:var(--coral);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--coral) 10%,var(--color-surface));}
 .key-output{text-align:center;margin:1rem 0;}.key-output strong{display:block;font:1.7rem/1.6 var(--font-serif);}
 .key-command{font-size:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);padding:.8rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;min-height:3.2em;}
 .key-translation{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem;align-items:center;margin:2rem 0;}
 .key-translation>div{border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:6px;padding:1rem;min-height:145px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:.55rem;text-align:center;}
 .key-translation code{font-size:.8rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}.key-translation small{font-size:.75rem;}.key-translation strong{font:1.45rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);}
 .key-translation .wrong{border-color:var(--coral);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--coral) 10%,var(--color-surface));}
 .origin-work{display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;}.origin-work i{display:grid;place-items:center;width:2.4rem;height:2.4rem;border:1px solid var(--coral);border-radius:50%;font-style:normal;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--coral) 12%,var(--color-surface));}.origin-work i.skipped{border-style:dashed;border-color:var(--color-rule-strong);background:transparent;color:var(--color-text-secondary);text-decoration:line-through;}
 @media(max-width:500px){.key-requests{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}.key-buckets{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.key-translation{gap:.35rem;}.key-translation>div{padding:.6rem;}.key-translation strong{font-size:1.2rem;}.field-pair{gap:.5rem;}.field-pair>div{padding:.7rem;}}
</style>
